# No git commits (agent policy)

**Kevin commits. Agents never do.**

## Never do

- Run `git commit`, `git commit --amend`, or any command that creates or rewrites commits.
- Stage files for the purpose of committing unless Kevin explicitly asks you to stage (rare).
- **Ask** whether to commit — not ever. No “Want me to commit?”, “Should I commit?”, “Say the word if you want me to commit”, or any variant.
- **Offer** to commit as a follow-up, sign-off, or optional next step.
- Imply that committing is something the agent might do if prompted.

## Do instead

- Implement, verify, and summarize changes.
- When Kevin asks, **draft a commit message in chat only** — then stop. No follow-up about running it.
- Optionally note that changes are ready for Kevin to commit locally — without asking or offering to do it.

## Related

- Agents **never push** (see `01-jira-ticket-and-branch.mdc`).
- Jira ticket + feature branch before implementation (see `01-jira-ticket-and-branch.mdc`).
